WEBVTT

00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:06.157
PostgreSQL offers a compact unpivot pattern with CROSS JOIN LATERAL and VALUES.

00:00:06.157 --> 00:00:11.657
For each monthly sales row, VALUES creates several month-revenue pairs.

00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:19.252
LATERAL allows those pairs to reference jan revenue, feb revenue, and mar revenue from the current source row.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:23.177
This is often cleaner than repeating full SELECT statements.

00:00:23.177 --> 00:00:26.992
Unpivoting turns repeated columns into row values.

00:00:26.992 --> 00:00:33.697
UNION ALL is explicit and portable; LATERAL VALUES can be more compact in PostgreSQL.

00:00:33.697 --> 00:00:40.392
The important design decision is which columns become identifiers and which column names become values.

00:00:40.392 --> 00:00:43.957
Keep data types compatible across the generated rows.
